CARI4D FoundationPose export: record "no observed object pixels" as NaN, not inf; mark such tracked frames unreliable.
Upstream: nvidia-isaac/video_to_data reconstruction/modules/v2d_cari4d/lib/cari4d/prep/run_foundationpose_mhr_export.py
  (main 12c36fb = runtime pin 8c778f9 for this module), md5 c93056318b5320eb028a170d4ae482b6; patched md5 556a32239f14f8b87a137f1edec26514.
Why: in --register-first-then-track every frame after registration is tracked and measured; a frame whose object
mask minus human mask is empty keeps centroid_distance = inf, and validate_foundationpose_selection_arrays rejects
the whole episode after all frames are tracked (ep01-ep04 of Tier 3). Downstream reads only frames/obj_pose_world.
Applied by stages/recovery/tier3/t3_cari4d_ep.sh (bind-mounted over the image's copy); upstream source unchanged.

